       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 50 mg is far above the usual amlodipine dose. The standard range is 2.5 to 10 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the maximum for most adults. Entering 50 mg could cause severe hypotension.\n\nIt may be a typo for 5 mg or 10 mg, or the intended dose may be different. Please confirm the intended dose with the prescribing physician. Once you or the prescriber confirm the dose, I can enter the order as amlodipine, by mouth, once daily.\n\nAlso, because medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, the order should be entered or co-signed by the responsible clinician, not by me or by you in a non-clinical role."
